<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson wins South Africa network order.</title>
<headline>Ericsson wins South Africa network order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecommunications group Ericsson said on Wednesday it had won a contract from Telkom South Africa to supply small and medium capacity radios for its network.</p>
<p>The tender calls for around 3,000 radio terminals over a two-year period.</p>
<p>The radios will be used in the fixed network as well as providing the backbone for the cellular network operator's network in both rural and urban areas, Ericsson said in a statement.</p>
<p>No financial details of the contract were released.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
